## 5. Delegation

- Depth 2 (OD-04): PM → specialist → allow-listed specialist. A depth-2 specialist may not launch another subagent.
- A specialist may delegate only to its allow-list in `docs/harness/agent-specifications.md` §1.4 as encoded in `.opencode/agents/`.
- **No delegation to `general` or `explore`** (OD-21): built-in subagents inherit broad base permissions and bypass role limits.
- Maximum two attempts and one re-delegation; then escalate to the PM.
- Delegation never transfers phase approval, merge, deploy, destructive data, security-risk acceptance, requirements/AC approval, or review of the delegator's own work.
- Every delegation uses a task envelope: issue, objective, inputs, constraints, deliverable, DoD, evidence. The PM verifies evidence, not claims.

## 6. PR review authority (OD-19)

- Agent PR verdicts are **advisory**: prefix `[advisory:<role>]` and use `APPROVE`, `REQUEST CHANGES`, or `BLOCK`.
- A GitHub `approve` review is permitted only with a distinct agent identity (GitHub App/bot). Without it, advisory comments only — hard-denied by policy regardless of any approval.
- An agent verdict never satisfies branch protection, owner-required review, phase approval, security-risk acceptance, or merge authority. Only the owner merges. No agent approves its own work or a PR it authored.
- Agent verdicts are limited to code/docs PRs. Phase-gate, status/decision, harness/governance, release/production, destructive-data, and risk-acceptance PRs are owner-only.

